Error [jet.DispatchHoleCandidatePattern]: A pattern or range arm needs a plain `if subject == {` table
  --> Tests/UI/e0948_dispatch_hole_range_arm.jet:5:9
    |
  5 |         2..4 -> print("small factor")
    |         ^^^^
 Why: A hole table puts each arm's candidate in its `<>` as a value, and a pattern or range is not a value; only a plain table matches each arm against its subject
 Fix: Write the table as `if subject == {`, or write this arm's candidate as a value
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0948
